WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.660
- Today I'm getting my dream pet.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.000
For as long as I can remember,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.430
my dream pet has been a potbellied pig.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.550
And today, I get to take care of one.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.856
I'm taking care of a
pig named Hamlet today.

00:00:13.856 --> 00:00:15.640
I'm gonna meet her at her house,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.677
learn her routine with her family,

00:00:17.677 --> 00:00:19.990
and then we're gonna
bring her back to my house

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.264
and see how we do alone together.

00:00:22.264 --> 00:00:24.764
(happy music)

00:00:26.174 --> 00:00:27.186
- I'm Melanie.

00:00:27.186 --> 00:00:28.200
- And I'm Michael.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.690
- And we're Hamlet's humans.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.506
I got her when she was six weeks old.

00:00:32.506 --> 00:00:37.506
When I bought her from a breeder,
she was a micro, mini pig.

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.960
Soon after, I found out
there's no such thing.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.400
She's a potbellied pig.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.250
- What's the difference
between taking care

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.950
of a dog and taking care of a pig?

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.450
- Their behavior is not the same.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.108
A lot of people think
that you just train a pig

00:00:49.108 --> 00:00:52.153
how you would train a dog,
but pigs are very different.

00:00:52.153 --> 00:00:53.530
They remember things.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.334
Sometimes they'll seek
revenge, and pee in rooms.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.940
- So they're really smart and they like to

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.432
seek revenge, which I relate to.

00:01:01.432 --> 00:01:03.100
- You know, she gets into everything,

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.918
she's very curious, she
needs constant attention.

00:01:05.918 --> 00:01:08.603
We can't leave anything
out that smells good.

00:01:08.603 --> 00:01:12.050
They need to get to know you,
because they're naturally

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.600
prey, they're kind of weary
of new people and new things.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.278
- This table is all the stuff that

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.512
she needs to live her best life.

00:01:20.512 --> 00:01:22.200
- So I made a checklist for you.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.300
Snacks is first on the checklist.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.390
Pumpkin, carrot.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:26.487
I have an outfit for her.

00:01:26.487 --> 00:01:29.328
The dressing started
because of her fair skin.

00:01:29.328 --> 00:01:30.747
It was easier.
- I relate to that.

00:01:30.747 --> 00:01:32.533
I relate to Hamlet more than I expected.

00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:33.490
(Melanie laughs)

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.550
- Then we have a harness and a leash.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.460
A scratcher, very important.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.511
Pigs love belly rubs.

00:01:38.511 --> 00:01:40.079
You are gonna do Instagram.

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:42.731
Do you want the pink car?

00:01:42.731 --> 00:01:43.780
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:44.613
- [Melanie] Okay.

00:01:44.613 --> 00:01:46.322
- Let's pack her up and take her home.

00:01:46.322 --> 00:01:48.142
So here's Hamlet.

00:01:48.142 --> 00:01:50.475
(pig oinks)

00:01:51.971 --> 00:01:53.821
You okay?

00:01:53.821 --> 00:01:55.510
You wanna go on an adventure?

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:56.876
Now I have my dream pet for a day.

00:01:56.876 --> 00:01:58.270
It's happening.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:01:59.390
It's really happening.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:02.349
We're on our own now, and hopefully,

00:02:02.349 --> 00:02:04.640
I make a best friend today.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.473
Okay, we are home.

00:02:05.473 --> 00:02:07.690
Putting you down is hard.

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:09.469
You're so heavy.

00:02:09.469 --> 00:02:11.398
Oh God, oh God, oh God.

00:02:11.398 --> 00:02:12.404
Okay?

00:02:12.404 --> 00:02:13.810
We're good.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.467
I think she's finding crumbs.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:19.484
She might like me more, knowing
that I have food around.

00:02:19.484 --> 00:02:21.984
(happy music)

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.836
We're taking a tour.

00:02:24.836 --> 00:02:26.730
We're in my bedroom now.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.610
She's cleaning the floor,
and I appreciate that.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:31.090
She's a good roommate.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.970
I can't believe I have
a pig in my bedroom.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.580
I'm gonna put her litter box in a corner,

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.180
'cause I know she likes corners.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.050
She's very messy.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.588
- [Woman] Uh oh, she's on your carpet.

00:02:43.588 --> 00:02:44.470
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.880
- Let me wipe you.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:46.868
Oh, she's mad.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.684
(pig oinks)
Oh God. Oh no.

00:02:48.684 --> 00:02:51.450
You graze and I will wipe.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.362
Thank you.

00:02:52.362 --> 00:02:54.128
Aw, she was good.

00:02:54.128 --> 00:02:55.577
She's like a little kid, but you need to

00:02:55.577 --> 00:02:57.797
wipe their face because who knows

00:02:57.797 --> 00:03:00.930
what's on it, and she's
just like "No, no."

00:03:02.211 --> 00:03:03.600
You want water?

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:07.550
I feel like she's having a good time.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:09.005
I'm gonna take her out to lunch

00:03:09.005 --> 00:03:11.218
because I'm a good friend and pet owner,

00:03:11.218 --> 00:03:15.520
but I need to get her harness
on so that she's safe.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.178
Her mom told me it's
really hard to put on her

00:03:18.178 --> 00:03:22.670
because it's super tight,
she doesn't really enjoy it,

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.540
so I'm gonna just kinda do what

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.650
she told me to do, which
is chase her down and

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.868
sort of, like, get her head in there.

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.642
I'm a little nervous.

00:03:30.642 --> 00:03:31.475
Hamlet.

00:03:35.611 --> 00:03:37.590
You okay?

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.970
I think that means she's fine.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:40.803
We did it though.

00:03:40.803 --> 00:03:42.262
We did it.

00:03:42.262 --> 00:03:43.330
Wanna go to lunch?

00:03:46.162 --> 00:03:51.162
I'm trying to eat lunch and my pet pig

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.725
is making a great escape from her

00:03:53.725 --> 00:03:56.591
stroller, and I'm proud of her.

00:03:56.591 --> 00:03:58.300
That's crafty.

00:04:01.035 --> 00:04:02.616
You wanna go home?

00:04:02.616 --> 00:04:06.650
(bouncy electronic music)

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:09.030
That lunch was not super comfortable,

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.374
mostly because people just kept coming up,

00:04:11.374 --> 00:04:15.640
which is fine, but it was
also a little bit intrusive

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.696
in a way that it was like,
they were touching her

00:04:18.696 --> 00:04:22.599
and I just got a little nervous
that she might get nervous.

00:04:22.599 --> 00:04:25.535
One of my friends is stopping
by just to drop something off.

00:04:25.535 --> 00:04:30.247
She doesn't realize what's
in my apartment right now.

00:04:30.247 --> 00:04:33.705
You weren't planning on hanging
out, but just come inside.

00:04:33.705 --> 00:04:34.610
- [Lizz] Should I be scared?

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:35.443
- [Kelly] No.

00:04:35.443 --> 00:04:36.561
- Oh my God, what?

00:04:36.561 --> 00:04:37.730
What is that?

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:38.975
- [Kelly] That's my pig.

00:04:38.975 --> 00:04:40.264
Her name is Hamlet.

00:04:40.264 --> 00:04:42.030
You can go over to her.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.920
Look.
- Oh my God.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:44.753
- We're friends now.

00:04:44.753 --> 00:04:45.586
If you sit.

00:04:45.586 --> 00:04:46.981
Jump.

00:04:46.981 --> 00:04:48.550
Ah, good girl.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:49.650
Okay.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.280
- Oh my God, how is she--

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.863
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:55.984 --> 00:04:57.370
She just eats it?

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.150
- Okay, bye.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.182
- [Lizz] She's bringing it
all over the place, too.

00:05:04.182 --> 00:05:06.682
(happy music)

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.830
- I'm gonna try to put on her outfit,

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.280
because I promised her owners that I

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:14.820
would do an Instagram for her,

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.938
because that's part of her daily routine.

00:05:16.938 --> 00:05:19.954
And this is going to be interesting.

00:05:19.954 --> 00:05:22.537
(bouncy music)

00:05:26.498 --> 00:05:28.572
Turns out you really need
to get in there with this,

00:05:28.572 --> 00:05:30.882
so I figured out how to get it

00:05:30.882 --> 00:05:32.620
and I think I pulled it through.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.530
Now she's just really happy on my

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.260
lap, which makes me really happy.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.770
I've had a full pig on my lap before.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.010
This is something I've always wanted.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.516
Okay, she has her pink car here.

00:05:45.516 --> 00:05:48.550
We brought it with us for this Instagram

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:51.329
opportunity that I was tasked with.

00:05:51.329 --> 00:05:54.060
But we're so happy right
now just like this.

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.260
Do we really have to go?

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:57.487
Yes? Okay.

00:05:57.487 --> 00:06:00.662
I'm gonna put on one more little
piece of clothing for her.

00:06:00.662 --> 00:06:03.240
Now she looks beautiful, but she

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.140
always looks beautiful, let's be real.

00:06:06.305 --> 00:06:08.250
This is kind of hard.

00:06:12.262 --> 00:06:14.715
So I feel like this is
a good stopping point

00:06:14.715 --> 00:06:17.546
because I'm scared to go any further.

00:06:17.546 --> 00:06:20.713
(jazzy trumpet music)

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.586
Today was amazing.

00:06:29.586 --> 00:06:31.876
I got my dream pet for a full day.

00:06:31.876 --> 00:06:33.940
We did a bunch of stuff.

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.580
And now ending the day
kind of just in my bed,

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.514
where I would sleep with my pet pig.

00:06:38.514 --> 00:06:42.580
Just to have her here burrowing
in my blanket in my room,

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:45.310
it feels really special,
and it's something

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:48.811
that I didn't know if I
would ever get to do, so.

00:06:48.811 --> 00:06:51.520
I will say that taking care of pigs

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.838
is definitely not for everyone.

00:06:52.838 --> 00:06:57.378
You really do need space, you
need time, you need grass,

00:06:57.378 --> 00:07:01.570
and they just deserve all
the attention they get,

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:03.128
but they do need a lot of attention.

00:07:03.128 --> 00:07:05.950
I might just stay here
the rest of the day,

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:09.190
the rest of my life,
so you guys can go now.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:10.447
Bye.

00:07:10.447 --> 00:07:13.030
(twangy music)

